# Paths the bundled secret scanner does not read. One substring per line; any
# path containing it is skipped. Blank lines and lines starting with # ignored.
#
# An entry here is a claim that what lives at that path only looks like a
# credential — a test fixture, a documented example, a key that was generated
# for a demo and never worked anywhere. Write the reason beside it, because the
# next person to read this file will be deciding whether to trust you.
#
# Never allowlist a real credential. Rotate it instead. An allowlisted secret is
# one nobody will ever be warned about again, which is strictly worse than one
# nobody has noticed yet.
#
# For example:
#   test/fixtures/    # deliberately invalid keys, used to test the scanner
